    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0577" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg469"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Señor Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose with reference
                    to your note of the 17th instant, a copy of letter from the Secretary of War of
                    the 20th instant, and of the telegrams which he communicates of the 18th and
                    19th instant, by which it appears that U. S. troops visited San Elizario but
                    found no armed party there of any kind.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>





